<%#
  The icon set, per sport (#319).

  Was fourteen copies of the same four <link> tags, which is why the hardwood
  assets shipped in #308 and then went nowhere: adding a sport meant editing
  every view, and nobody notices the problem until two leagues are open in two
  tabs — at which point both say "football" and it is very annoying.

  `viewerSport` comes from server.js off the viewer's league, defaulting to
  football for a signed-out page.
%>
<%# Only basketball differs, so the test is for basketball and everything else
    — unset, signed out, a sport nobody has added yet — gets the football mark.
    An explicit `|| 'football'` default read as load-bearing and could not be
    made to fail a test, because an empty sport already yields this suffix. %>
<% var _sfx = (typeof viewerSport !== 'undefined' && viewerSport) === 'basketball' ? '-hardwood' : ''; %>
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/images/favicon<%= _sfx %>.svg" />
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/images/favicon<%= _sfx %>-32.png" />
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/images/favicon<%= _sfx %>-16.png" />
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/images/apple-touch-icon<%= _sfx %>.png" />
